Therefore we can state the 
\begin{proposition} \label{prop:correspondence_DDKS_covers}
 A finite group $G$ admits a diagonal double Kodaira structure of type $(b, \, n)$ if and only if there is a surjective group homomorphism 
\begin{equation} \label{eq:varphi}
\varphi \colon \mathsf{P}_2(\Sigma_b) \to G
\end{equation}
such that $\mathsf{z}=\varphi(A_{12})$ has order $n\geq 2$. Note that the last condition implies that $\varphi$ does not factor through $\pi_1(\Sigma_b \times \Sigma_b)$. 
\end{proposition}
