theorem.content:
\label{thm:ExistenceOfChords}
Consider a Hamiltonian $H$ as in \eqref{DefH} and fix $q_0,q_1 \in \mathbb{R}^2$, such that $|q_0|,|q_1|\leq R_1$. Denote by $B(R_1)$ a ball in $\mathbb{R}^2$ with radius $R_1$ and center at the origin.
If one of the following conditions is satisfied:
\begin{enumerate}[label=\arabic*.]
\item We choose energy value
\begin{equation}\label{CondC}
c> \max\left\lbrace \sqrt[3]{32a^2}, \sqrt{4a\left(3 R_1+2\sqrt[3]{2a}\right)}\right\rbrace,
\end{equation}
\item We choose the energy value $c>\sqrt{2aR_1}$ and, additionally, the potential function $V$ is rotationally invariant outside of $B(R_1)$, i.e. for all $r\geq R_1$ we have $\partial_\theta V(r,\theta)=0$,
\end{enumerate}
then there exists a solution $(v,\eta)\in W^{1,2}([0,1], T^*\mathbb{R}^2)\times\mathbb{R}$ to \eqref{Def(v,eta)}, such that\linebreak $v([0,1])\subseteq T^*B(R_1)$.

