 Since we already proved the existence of $P$-states on $\mathscr{Q}(H)$ under the continuum hypothesis, it suffices to show there is an irreducible representation of $\mathscr{Q}(H)$ which fails infinite transitivity. In fact, such a representation exists in ZFC.

\begin{introthm}\label{counter}
