\end{equation}$_{\lambda}$ does not admit weak solutions
		for every $\lambda>\Lambda$;
		\item[B)] problem the equation above$_{\lambda}$ admits at least one weak solution for every $\lambda \in (0,\Lambda]$;
		\item[C)] problem the equation above$_{\lambda}$ admits at least two weak solutions for every $0<\lambda<\Lambda$.
	\end{itemize}

