Let $C$ and $E$ 

be two circles such that the ratio of their radii is rational and such that a triangle
with rational sides has  $C$ as circumcircle and  $E$ as one of its excircles. Then there exist infinitely
many rational non-similar triangles with rational sides that have  $C$ as circumcircle and  $E$ as excircle.
\end{cor}
