ref_dict.thm: ZR:
\begin{thm} \label{thm: ZR}
    For a $\mathbb{Z}^d$ product density $g(z) = \prod_{i=1}^d g_i(z_i)$, if $g_i$ are log-concave, then $f*g$ is log-supermodular if $f$ is log-supermodular.
\end{thm}

ref_dict.cor: ZR:
\begin{cor} \label{cor: ZR}
    For $g$ the standard Gaussian density on $\mathbb{R}^d$, and $f$ log-supermodular,
    $f*g$ is also log-supermodular.
\end{cor}

