For $A \subset \R^d$ and $a \in A$, the following are equivalent.
\begin{enumerate}
\item[(i)]  $  \reach(A,a) > 0.$
\item[(ii)]  There exists $\delta>0$ such that  $A \cap \overline{B}(a,\delta)$ has positive reach.
\item [(iii)] 
There exists a  set  $C$ and $\omega>0$ such that  $\reach C>0$ and $A \cap B(a, \omega)= C \cap B(a, \omega)$.
