\begin{proof}
Since every $Q \in \Rad(S^m)$ can be written as $Q = Q_1 \times \cdots \times Q_m$ with $Q_i \in \Rad(S)$ for $1\leq i \leq m$, it follows from \cite[Lemma 2.3 (b)]{NT11} that
\begin{align*}
