\begin{lemma}\label{comparable}
		Let $G$ be a graph.  
		There is an algorithm to obtain an induced subgraph $G'$ of $G$ in $O(|V(G)|+|E(G)|)$ time such that $G'$ has no comparable pair and $G$ is 3-colorable if and only if $G'$ is 3-colorable. 
		Moreover, any 3-coloring of $G'$ can be extended to a 3-coloring of $G$ in $O(|V(G)|+|E(G)|)$ time. 
	\end{lemma}

