Let $Z:[r_{0},r_{1}] \rightarrow \mathbb{R}$ be a nonnegative and bounded function; let $\vartheta \in (0,1)$ and $C_{1},C_{2},\chi > 0$ be numbers. Assume that
\begin{equation*}
Z(\varrho_{0}) \le \vartheta Z(\varrho_{1}) + \frac{C_{1}}{(\varrho_{1}-\varrho_{0})^{\chi}} + C_{2}
\end{equation*}
holds for every choice of $\varrho_{0}$ and $\varrho_{1}$ such that $r_{0} \le \varrho_{0} < \varrho_{1} \le r_{1}$. Then the following inequality holds with $c\equiv c(\vartheta,\chi)>0$:
