\begin{theorem}[Liouville theorem]\label{Liouville theorem}
Let \( (M^n, g) \), \( n \ge 3 \), be a complete, locally conformally flat manifold with nonnegative scalar curvature.  
If \( \Phi : M^n \to S^n \) is a conformal map, then \( \Phi \) is injective and the boundary \( \partial \Phi(M) \) has zero Newtonian capacity (i.e.,  $2$-capacity).
\end{theorem}

