[Main Theorem] \label{thm:main}
For $n \geq 1$, every positive solution $u$ to \eqref{eqn:cr_yamabe} is a Jerison–Lee bubble, that is,
\begin{equation*}
u(z,t) = K\bigl| t + i|z|^2 + \mu \cdot z + \kappa \bigr|^{-\frac{Q-2}{2}},
