\label{thm:Cd-main}
For every $d \geq 1$ and every finite set $A\subset \mathbb{R}^m$ with exponential Freiman dimension $d$, we have 
\begin{equation} \label{eq:main-tight}
  |A+A|\geq C_d(|A|-2^d)+3^d,
\end{equation}
where
\[
  C_d \;=\;
  \begin{cases}
    2\bigl(\tfrac32\bigr)^{d-1}, & d \le 5,\\[4pt]
    2^{d/2+1} - 1, & d \ge 6 \text{ even},\\[4pt]
    3\cdot 2^{(d-1)/2} - \tfrac32, & d \ge 7 \text{ odd}.
  \end{cases}
\]

