ref_dict.thm:clique_classification:
\begin{theorem}\label{thm:clique_classification}
For any clique $\mathcal K=\{P_1,\dots,P_m\}$ with $m\ge 1$ in $\B_k(G)$, exactly one of the following holds:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item $\mathcal K=\{P_1,P_2,P_3\}$ is a cyclic $T$-triangle;
    \item $\mathcal K=\{P_1,P_2,P_3\}$  is a radial $T$-triangle;
    \item $\mathcal K=\{P_1,P_2,P_3,P_4\}$  is a split $T$-tetrahedron; 
    \item $\mathcal K=\{P_1,P_2,P_3,P_4\}$ is a fused $T$-tetrahedron; or 
    \item $\mathcal K=\{P_1,\dots,P_m\}$ is an $S$-clique.
\end{enumerate} 
\end{theorem}

