\begin{thm}\label{mainthm}
Suppose that $\Sigma$ is a smooth, projective, geometrically connected curve of genus $g$ defined over $k=\R$, and suppose that $\Sigma(\R)$ is a union of $b+1$ circles, with $b\geq 0$. Then 
$$P_t(M_r^d)  =  (-t)^{(g-1)r^2+1} A_{g,r,d} (-t, -t^{\frac{1}{2}}, -t^{\frac{1}{2}},  ..., -t^{\frac{1}{2}}, -1,-1,..,-1) $$ 
where  $(g-b)$-many entries equal $-t^{\frac{1}{2}}$ and $b$-many equal $-1$. 
\end{thm}

